Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.620 --> 00:00:08.019 align:start position:0%
 
[Music]  [Music]  heartland is ubisoft's new free-to-play  spin-off from the division universe  very little has been shared from the  studio but industry insider tom  henderson has been sharing information  that has been assisting in keeping the  interest alive  previously he has provided information  on heartland that is at least given some  sort of insight on the type of game  we'll be seeing released hopefully  sometime soon  heartland is based in the small town  setting of silver creek in the state of  new york  much like the base games there will be a  base of operations where players can  customize loadouts match make for  lobbies sell previously extracted loot  buy upgrades and new weapons  there will be classes that can be chosen  from that will provide unique talents  and perks like weapon expert medic and  survivalist  previously we had been told about two  game modes storm and excursion  excursion is a pve mode pitting players  against ai it has been described as a  way to prepare agents for the storm mode  the description provided says explore  alongside other friendly agents to  prepare the world for the incoming storm  storm is essentially the same thing but  it is pve vp  players should recognize this from the  dark zone that is present in both the  division and its sequel  however in the last day or so there have  been further updates released heartlands  will now feature four game modes  excursion storm nightfall and hunt  as stated earlier excursion is a pve  mode that is aimed at getting you  prepared for storm  in this mode players need to scavenge  loot explore and survive against enemy  ai with the objective of extracting from  the map via helicopter  storm heartland's flagship game mode  this is pretty much excursion except  with other players as well as ai  teams are composed of three players  where they can explore loot and scavenge  the large open world map  the gameplay could be compared to escape  from tarkov or hunt showdown where the  goal is to survive loot and extract from  silver creek to your base of operations  the aim is to earn more powerful gear to  take on greater challenges  as there are other players about these  upgrades will help you be better  prepared for these encounters  the map is a large open world where  players can explore and find loot dotted  throughout  much like the division you'll find loot  in five different rarities gray green  blue purple and gold  another feature of the map that is  relatively common in these br style  games is the release of deadly gas  around the map  this could be the virus similar to the  contaminated areas that we find in the  base game or perhaps it could be  something like dc 62 which was released  in washington dc  however rather than spreading from the  outside of the map and slowly creeping  in these contaminated areas can pop up  anywhere  in order to avoid being downed by this  players can craft gas mask filters in  order to survive gas-ridden areas  nightfall is the third heartland mode  that is an objective-based pve mode  just like with storm players need to  loot up survive and extract your base of  operations  nightfall however is a little different  with added layers to increase the  difficulty of the mode this mode  requires players to complete objectives  throughout the playthrough  some of these objectives include  deploying beacons tracking down targets  and collecting agent data  unlike storm players cannot extract with  a helicopter and instead need to extract  via an extraction point on foot at the  edge of the map  the catch players cannot extract from  silver creek at nightfall and need to  survive the night against the ai called  vultures  sadly not too much is known about hunt  but sources have suggested that this  mode is more pvp-based with no ai on the  map  in addition to these new modes sources  have confirmed several other key details  including that the division heartland  will feature cross play also the  inventory and gear system has had a huge  overhaul making it more familiar to what  we're used to in the division 1 and 2.  i mean this is a free to play game and a  lot of pve players have stated that they  have absolutely no interest in this  because it has been stated that this is  primarily focused on pvp  but with this news update there are now  a couple of pve options out there and  it's free so if you're a fan of the  franchise what do you have to lose in  trying it out i'm personally waiting to  see how this will expand on the universe  especially from a lower point of view  and if it doesn't i'm sure i'll be able  to fill in the gaps either way i'll be  jumping in to give it a go  yes obviously being free to play there  will be a bunch of micro transactions  and i know this is a dirty word and all  but the other games have shown that they  focus more around vanity items rather  than pay to win options so until i'm  showing otherwise i'm not concerned  about this  anyway this was just a quick update as  i've stated before any work going into  the expansion of the division universe  i'm happy so fingers crossed we have  something good coming with heartland  thanks for watching cheers  [Applause]  [Music]  uh  [Music]

